{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00032",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 6.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.72,
      "end_seconds": 10.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.21,
      "end_seconds": 19.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "I wanted to get pressure in the face looked at. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.33,
      "end_seconds": 22.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.66,
      "end_seconds": 28.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "About... well, two days. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.58,
      "end_seconds": 36.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.32,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.26,
      "end_seconds": 50.57,
      "duration_seconds": 12.31,
      "text": "Well, a eight out of ten, I suppose. Bending forward definitely sets it off. Only steam, and it's not much. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.12,
      "end_seconds": 54.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Has there been a headache over your forehead too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.89,
      "end_seconds": 56.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.96,
      "end_seconds": 59.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Has there been a blocked nose too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.41,
      "end_seconds": 61.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Mm, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.86,
      "end_seconds": 63.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.17,
      "end_seconds": 69.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Well, I'd give it a three, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.71,
      "end_seconds": 75.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Have you had pressure in the face before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.22,
      "end_seconds": 80.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.53,
      "end_seconds": 84.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.48,
      "end_seconds": 89.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Oh, yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.57,
      "end_seconds": 94.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Have you had any nosebleeds, ear pain or swelling around the eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.11,
      "end_seconds": 99.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "No. None of those, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.69,
      "end_seconds": 103.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.4,
      "end_seconds": 105.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.98,
      "end_seconds": 116.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. So, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.49,
      "end_seconds": 121.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "I had a stent put in my heart two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.43,
      "end_seconds": 140.26,
      "duration_seconds": 16.83,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.04,
      "end_seconds": 143.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Um, okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.91,
      "end_seconds": 149.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.01,
      "end_seconds": 154.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Uh, no, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.68,
      "end_seconds": 159.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.31,
      "end_seconds": 172.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.6,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.28,
      "end_seconds": 176.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.76,
      "end_seconds": 191.9,
      "duration_seconds": 14.14,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had asthma, yes. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. Eczema, for nearly five years. I've got heart disease. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.36,
      "end_seconds": 200.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Okay, eczema, that's already on your record. Good to know. What medicines do you take regularly? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.3,
      "end_seconds": 207.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "I'm on Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. It's hydrocortisone cream, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.53,
      "end_seconds": 211.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.18,
      "end_seconds": 215.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I mean, no problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 216.45,
      "end_seconds": 223.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 16, blood pressure 123 over 74. Pulse is 83 beats a minute, temp 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.05,
      "end_seconds": 238.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.38,
      "text": "Okay, noted. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.32,
      "end_seconds": 242.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.95,
      "end_seconds": 257.71,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.85,
      "end_seconds": 263.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Uh, good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.88,
      "end_seconds": 276.0,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "From what you've told me, this looks most like sinusitis. The reason I say that is that the way you describe it fits together. Allergic rhinitis is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.99,
      "end_seconds": 279.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.78,
      "end_seconds": 295.04,
      "duration_seconds": 15.26,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with sinusitis do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pressure in the face for two days, and no swelling around the eyes or ear pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.13,
      "end_seconds": 298.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Yes, you know, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.87,
      "end_seconds": 302.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.64,
      "end_seconds": 304.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.05,
      "end_seconds": 343.05,
      "duration_seconds": 29.0,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. We should do an X-ray of the sinuses for sinusitis. Let's use saline nasal spray, three times a day, for one week. That should help with nasal congestion. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. I'll start you on amoxicillin-clavulanate, 625 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. That should help with sinusitis. Steam a couple of times a day and saline rinses will help clear things."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.97,
      "end_seconds": 361.68,
      "duration_seconds": 17.71,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 363.21,
      "end_seconds": 366.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.8,
      "end_seconds": 372.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.64,
      "end_seconds": 378.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "So, I take the amoxicillin-clavulanate, 625 milligrams, twice a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.03,
      "end_seconds": 384.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.88,
      "end_seconds": 389.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.39,
      "end_seconds": 391.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}